&#34;Who deserves to live more comfortably and luxuriously, to rest in soft chairs and sleep upon elastic mattresses, to have generous food served elegantly to tempt the appetite and strengthen the body, than she who purchases all these with her own toil?&#34; said the strange logician whose daughters were too used to her &#34;queer notions&#34; to be startled by them. &#34;I do not say that you will make money fast, or at once. I do contend that, saving rent, bookkeeper&#39;s and saleswoman&#39;s wages, as you will do, you ought to be able to clear your busi-ness and personal expenses the first year-if nothing more.&#34;


&#34;If the customers come,&#34; suggested Emma.


Mrs. Hiller nodded confidently. &#34;They will come! In the beginning, out of curiosity and the love of novelty. It will depend upon your skill whether they continue their custom.&#34;


